00:46:40,260 --> 00:46:44,220
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: usually experience such a deficit in their current account.

621
00:46:45,080 --> 00:46:48,180
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Now, how is this deficit being supported right now?

622
00:46:48,760 --> 00:46:51,980
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And here we point to very important structural flows,

623
00:46:51,980 --> 00:46:57,660
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: the OFW remittances, the receipts from our BPO industry,

624
00:46:58,320 --> 00:47:03,400
