3515
02:53:23,320 --> 02:53:30,600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: or 15.9%, covering interest payments and net lending to government corporations.

3516
02:53:31,340 --> 02:53:34,940
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Honoring these obligations protect the government's creditworthiness

3517
02:53:34,940 --> 02:53:39,000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and helps preserve access to financing for future investments.

3518
02:53:39,720 --> 02:53:44,100
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Our task is to maintain that balance, honoring our government's obligations

3519
02:53:44,100 --> 02:53:47,520
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: while continuing to fund what our people need.

3520
02:53:47,520 --> 02:53:54,000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: By recipient units, national government agencies will receive 4.332 trillion,

3521
02:53:54,340 --> 02:53:56,040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the largest share of the budget.

3522
02:53:56,460 --> 02:54:03,500
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: However, their allocation grows by only 4.5%, below the overall budget growth of 6%,

3523
02:54:03,500 --> 02:54:07,340
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: reflecting continued restraint in national government spending.

3524
02:54:08,020 --> 02:54:14,940
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Local government units will receive 1.533 trillion, including a 1.32 trillion NTA,

3525
02:54:14,940 --> 02:54:17,500
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: compared with around 1.1 million NTA.

3526
02:54:17,520 --> 02:54:24,920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This means roughly 129.3 billion more, or about 11%,

3527
02:54:24,920 --> 02:54:30,920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: will flow directly to LGUs to support devolved functions and frontline services.

3528
02:54:31,480 --> 02:54:38,920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: GOCCs will receive 220.5 billion, while 1.114 trillion will go to interest payments.

3529
02:54:39,480 --> 02:54:44,020
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: These allocations underscore an important feature of the 2027 budget.

3530
02:54:44,320 --> 02:54:47,500
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Resources are not concentrated solely at the national level,

3531
02:54:47,520 --> 02:54:50,960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: a substantial share is transferred to LGUs,

3532
02:54:51,400 --> 02:54:54,520
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: bringing our country's resources closer to the communities

3533
02:54:54,520 --> 02:54:59,120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: where many essential public services are delivered to our citizens.

3534
02:54:59,680 --> 02:55:04,100
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The same principle is also evident in the regional distribution of the budget.

3535
02:55:04,560 --> 02:55:10,520
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Of the proposed 7.2 trillion, 4.603 trillion, or 63.9%,

3536
02:55:10,520 --> 02:55:13,360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: is directly attributable to the regions.

3537
02:55:13,360 --> 02:55:16,360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The national capital region accounts for 1.112,

3538
02:55:17,520 --> 02:55:19,960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Luzon at 1.659 trillion,

3539
02:55:20,480 --> 02:55:23,280
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Visayas at 4.8 billion,

3540
02:55:23,780 --> 02:55:26,400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and Mindanao at 1.088 trillion.

3541
02:55:26,400 --> 02:55:32,880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The remaining 2.597 trillion, or 36.1%, is non-regionalized,

3542
02:55:33,320 --> 02:55:38,760
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: consisting of 1.983 trillion pesos in nationwide allocations

3543
02:55:38,760 --> 02:55:43,400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and 613.8 billion in central office allocations.

3544
02:55:44,920 --> 02:55:46,440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We would like to clarify,

3545
02:55:46,440 --> 02:55:50,080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the important distinction of nationwide from Metro Manila.

3546
02:55:50,640 --> 02:55:54,720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Nationwide allocations pertain to funds that are still to be distributed

3547
02:55:54,720 --> 02:55:58,420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to various regions of the departments and agencies,

3548
02:55:58,960 --> 02:56:03,720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: as this cannot yet be geographically assigned at the time the NEP was prepared.

3549
02:56:04,360 --> 02:56:09,580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Ultimately, the majority of the budget is intended to reach our regions and communities.

3550
02:56:09,940 --> 02:56:11,720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: That is what we mean when we say,

3551
02:56:11,720 --> 02:56:14,040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: bawat bayan makikinabang.

3552
02:56:14,600 --> 02:56:16,080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: With the overall framework,

3553
02:56:16,080 --> 02:56:18,220
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and priorities of the budget established,

3554
02:56:18,560 --> 02:56:22,400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: let us now turn to where our most significant investments will be directed,

3555
02:56:22,640 --> 02:56:26,080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and how this will translate into better outcomes for Filipinos.

3556
02:56:27,220 --> 02:56:31,100
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Education remains at the center of our investment in human capital.

3557
02:56:31,660 --> 02:56:38,700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The Department of Education will receive the highest allocation at 975.96 billion pesos,

3558
02:56:38,700 --> 02:56:44,040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: while 176.5 billion is provided for higher education

3559
02:56:44,040 --> 02:56:46,040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to broaden access to quality,

3560
02:56:46,520 --> 02:56:48,440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and affordable tertiary learning.

3561
02:56:49,020 --> 02:56:53,200
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Taken together with the other components of government education spending,

3562
02:56:53,200 --> 02:57:00,020
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: our proposed investment in basic and higher education reaches 1.326 trillion,

3563
02:57:00,360 --> 02:57:03,400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: equivalent to nearly 4% of the GDP,

3564
02:57:03,880 --> 02:57:09,140
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and effectively reaching the lower bound of the UNESCO Education 2030 benchmark

3565
02:57:09,140 --> 02:57:14,640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of 4-6% of GDP for education spending for the second time.

3566
02:57:15,080 --> 02:57:16,060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The difference between the two is that, for the first time,

3567
02:57:16,060 --> 02:57:26,060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: between 1.314 trillion reflected in the President's budget and the 1.326 trillion presented during the DBCC briefing at the House

3568
02:57:26,060 --> 02:57:36,240
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: is due to the inclusion of the Tier 2 projections for BARM education agencies which were not yet available when the budget message was prepared and printed.

3569
02:57:36,240 --> 02:57:45,700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: By the time of the House briefing, these projections were already available and were therefore included in computing the overall education sector figure.

3570
02:57:46,060 --> 02:57:51,180
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, to be clear, there was no change in the 2027 NEP after its submission.

3571
02:57:51,700 --> 02:57:56,380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The difference simply reflects the more complete BARM education sector figures,

3572
02:57:56,840 --> 02:57:59,640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: which is available at the time of the DBCC presentation.

3573
02:58:00,460 --> 02:58:04,640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This is consistent with how we view education as a national commitment,

3574
02:58:04,640 --> 02:58:14,440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: one that leaves no learner behind, whether served by our national education agencies, in BARM, and in all communities across the country.

3575
02:58:14,980 --> 02:58:16,040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: More importantly,

3576
02:58:16,060 --> 02:58:20,000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: these allocations translate into specific investments.

3577
02:58:20,560 --> 02:58:27,260
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We are proposing 12.09 billion for the expanded career progression system for public school teachers,

3578
02:58:27,720 --> 02:58:32,680
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: an increase of almost 6 billion or 96.6% from the current year.

3579
02:58:32,960 --> 02:58:37,260
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This is to support the reclassification and career advancement of our teachers.

3580
02:58:37,260 --> 02:58:46,020
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Another 10.36 billion allocation next year will also sustain the 10,000 peso teaching allowance under the Kabalika,

3581
02:58:46,900 --> 02:58:49,180
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: For tertiary education,

3582
02:58:49,660 --> 02:58:58,820
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: 61.1 billion is provided for the universal access to quality tertiary education across state universities and colleges,

3583
02:58:59,160 --> 02:59:00,240
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: CHED and TESDA,

3584
02:59:00,680 --> 02:59:04,960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: supporting free higher education, tertiary education subsidies,

3585
02:59:05,520 --> 02:59:08,060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and free technical vocational education.

3586
02:59:08,700 --> 02:59:09,140
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Ultimately,

3587
02:59:09,700 --> 02:59:13,620
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the significance of the 1.326 trillion peso budget

3588
02:59:13,620 --> 02:59:15,620
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: will not be measured by the amount of education.

3589
02:59:15,620 --> 02:59:15,700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This is to support the development of the education sector,

3590
02:59:15,700 --> 02:59:15,760
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and to support the development of the education sector.

3591
02:59:15,760 --> 02:59:30,640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: It will be measured by better learning outcomes, better supported teachers, wider access to education and training, and more opportunities for Filipino learners to build a future they rightfully deserve.

3592
02:59:31,760 --> 02:59:38,900
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The top 10 departments with the largest allocations account for 51.4% of the proposed budget.

3593
02:59:38,900 --> 03:00:03,030
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Apart from education, major allocations will go to public works and highways, health, interior and local government, national defense, transportation, agriculture, social welfare and development, higher education, and the judiciary, fully aligned with the administration's priorities and the Philippine development.

3594
03:00:03,040 --> 03:00:21,980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: On infrastructure, let me emphasize that infrastructure is more than just the DPWH budget. Under the Build Better More infrastructure program, the government is proposing 1.467 trillion pesos, equivalent to 4.4% of GDP for infrastructure in 2027.

3595
03:00:21,980 --> 03:00:34,220
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: These investments are distributed across public works, transportation, agriculture, education, defense, health, digital infrastructure, and other sectors.

3596
03:00:34,760 --> 03:00:43,360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Specifically, DPWH will receive 643.95 billion, or the second largest allocation among agencies.

3597
03:00:44,000 --> 03:00:50,680
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This is partly to support ongoing locally funded and foreign-assisted infrastructure flagship projects.

3598
03:00:50,680 --> 03:01:04,900
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Major projects include the Laguna Lakeshore Road Network Project at 35 billion, Bataan-Cavite Interlink Bridge Project at 22 billion, Davao City Bypass Construction Project Package 1 at 11.9 billion,

3599
03:01:05,480 --> 03:01:16,920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Cebu-Mactan Bridge and Coastal Road Construction Project at 8.5 billion, and Pasig-Marikina River Channel Improvement Project Phase 4 at 8.5 billion pesos.

3600
03:01:17,220 --> 03:01:19,920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Transportation is likewise a major priority.

3601
03:01:20,680 --> 03:01:26,400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: With 300.96 billion proposed for the DOTR and its attached agencies.

3602
03:01:26,400 --> 03:01:44,860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This includes 123.84 billion for the North-South Commuter Railway System, 67.44 billion for Phase 1 of the Metro Manila Subway Project, and 1.94 billion for the MRT Line 3 Rehabilitation Project.

3603
03:01:45,160 --> 03:01:46,880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Beyond Metro Manila,

3604
03:01:47,320 --> 03:01:50,660
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: 175.49 million is provided for the Cebu Bus Rapid Transit Project, and 15.08 billion for the Davao Public Transport Modernization Project.

3605
03:01:50,680 --> 03:02:11,880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We are also investing 8.99 billion in the new Cebu International Container Port Project, and 1.41 billion in the new Dumaguete Airport Development Project.

3606
03:02:11,880 --> 03:02:19,700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: These investments demonstrate that reducing travel time and logistics costs, connecting regional economies,

3607
03:02:19,700 --> 03:02:31,140
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: improving the movement of people and goods, and bringing more Filipinos within reach of jobs and economic opportunities are important priorities of this administration.

3608
03:02:31,900 --> 03:02:39,280
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Our other major investments pursue the same objective of improving people's security and quality of life.

3609
03:02:39,280 --> 03:02:49,680
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Across the agriculture sector, 261.7 billion will support food security, productivity, and the livelihood.

3610
03:02:49,700 --> 03:03:10,160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The proposed fiscal year 2027 budget continues to make quality healthcare more accessible, more affordable, and more responsive to the needs of every Filipino by allocating 353.8 billion for the health sector.

3611
03:03:10,160 --> 03:03:19,620
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We are providing 107.29 billion for the operations of DOH regional hospitals and other health facilities.

3612
03:03:19,700 --> 03:03:31,700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Along with 28.19 billion for DOH hospitals and Metro Manila to expand healthcare capacity, modernize facilities, and strengthen specialized medical services.

3613
03:03:33,000 --> 03:03:45,800
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This means more Filipinos can access quality healthcare closer to home, while those requiring highly specialized treatment continue to receive world-class care in our major public hospitals.

3614
03:03:45,920 --> 03:03:49,180
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: To further reduce what Filipino families,

3615
03:03:49,700 --> 03:03:53,020
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: from out of their own pockets when they are hospitalized,

3616
03:03:53,780 --> 03:03:57,980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: we are strengthening the implementation of the universal healthcare through PhilHealth

3617
03:03:57,980 --> 03:04:02,400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: with an allocation of 74.45 billion pesos.

3618
03:04:03,000 --> 03:04:07,820
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This will support the continued expansion of the PhilHealth's benefit packages,

3619
03:04:08,300 --> 03:04:14,080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: including the implementation of zero-balance billing in both DOH and LGU hospitals.

3620
03:04:14,080 --> 03:04:17,980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: From only six LGU hospitals this year,

3621
03:04:18,580 --> 03:04:26,120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: zero-balance billing will expand to 352 LGU hospitals nationwide next year,

3622
03:04:26,600 --> 03:04:33,420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: allowing millions more Filipinos to receive quality hospital care without worrying about the cost.

3623
03:04:33,940 --> 03:04:37,200
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: More importantly, this means that when illness strikes,

3624
03:04:37,700 --> 03:04:40,880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Filipino families can focus on their loved ones' recovery,

3625
03:04:40,880 --> 03:04:43,700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: not on how they will pay the hospital bill.

3626
03:04:44,080 --> 03:04:47,540
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This is our commitment to making quality healthcare more accessible,

3627
03:04:48,200 --> 03:04:51,760
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: more affordable, and more compassionate to every Filipino.

3628
03:04:52,360 --> 03:04:57,600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: For social protection, DSWD will receive 241 billion,

3629
03:04:58,140 --> 03:05:04,120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: including 99 billion for the implementation of the Pantawid Pamilyang Pilipino Program.

3630
03:05:04,540 --> 03:05:09,700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: For national defense, 328.8 billion is proposed,

3631
03:05:09,700 --> 03:05:13,700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: including 50 billion for the revised AFP modernization program

3632
03:05:14,080 --> 03:05:17,160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and 10 billion higher than the current year's level.

3633
03:05:17,720 --> 03:05:22,400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The Philippine Coast Guard will receive 45.51 billion,

3634
03:05:22,760 --> 03:05:28,060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: while 73.67 billion is proposed for the subsistence allowance

3635
03:05:28,060 --> 03:05:33,100
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of our military and uniformed personnel across concerned agencies.

3636
03:05:33,840 --> 03:05:38,380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: For the judiciary, 86.27 billion is included

3637
03:05:38,380 --> 03:05:43,340
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to support the administration of justice and access to judicial services.

3638
03:05:43,340 --> 03:05:47,800
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Consistent with the constitutional principle of judicial independence

3639
03:05:47,800 --> 03:05:52,080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and the provisions of the Judiciary Fiscal Autonomy Act,

3640
03:05:52,640 --> 03:06:00,000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the Supreme Court's original budget proposal has been incorporated into the fiscal year 2027 NEP,

3641
03:06:00,440 --> 03:06:05,700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: recognizing the judiciary's fiscal autonomy and constitutional mandate.

3642
03:06:06,300 --> 03:06:10,240
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Resilience is likewise integral to the 2027 budget.

3643
03:06:10,240 --> 03:06:13,240
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We are proposing 45.67 billion,

3644
03:06:13,340 --> 03:06:30,200
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: including 14.67 billion for the Disaster Rehabilitation and Reconstruction Assistance Program for LGUs and 1 billion for the People's Survival Fund.

3645
03:06:30,780 --> 03:06:36,000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Taken together, these investments reveal the broader purpose of the 2027 budget

3646
03:06:36,000 --> 03:06:40,980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to protect vulnerable Filipinos, strengthen human capital and food security,

3647
03:06:40,980 --> 03:06:43,020
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: build productive infrastructure,

3648
03:06:43,340 --> 03:06:44,640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: safeguard the nation,

3649
03:06:45,100 --> 03:06:46,120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: empower our region,

3650
03:06:46,640 --> 03:06:50,260
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and improve our ability to withstand future shocks.

3651
03:06:50,640 --> 03:06:54,240
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: That commitment extends directly to our local government units.

3652
03:06:54,240 --> 03:07:01,240
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: 1.32 trillion NTA gives LGUs greater resources to perform devolved functions,

3653
03:07:02,040 --> 03:07:08,060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: while 115.62 billion will support peace, self-governance,

3654
03:07:08,200 --> 03:07:13,180
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and long-term development in the Bangsamoro Autonomous Region in Muslim Mindanao.

3655
03:07:13,340 --> 03:07:19,240
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We are likewise proposing 58.53 billion for the Local Government Support Fund,

3656
03:07:19,360 --> 03:07:25,580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: covering financial assistance to LGUs, the Growth Equity Fund, and the Barangay Development Program.

3657
03:07:25,580 --> 03:07:32,700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: By strengthening local fiscal capacity, we bring resources and decision-making closer to communities

3658
03:07:32,700 --> 03:07:36,920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and give every region a stronger voice in national development.

3659
03:07:37,440 --> 03:07:41,720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This is what people-centered growth means, one that reaches every community,

3660
03:07:42,100 --> 03:07:42,580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: creates opportunities

3661
03:07:43,340 --> 03:07:44,440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for every Filipino,

3662
03:07:44,920 --> 03:07:50,400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and ensures that progress is broadly and fairly shared across the country.

3663
03:07:50,940 --> 03:07:57,420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: These are only some of the key priorities reflected in the proposed Fiscal Year 2027 National Budget.

3664
03:07:57,420 --> 03:08:02,060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: To provide a broader view of the programs and projects we seek to pursue,

3665
03:08:02,580 --> 03:08:06,780
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: we have also prepared a short video presentation that we can probably share later.

3666
03:08:07,440 --> 03:08:11,180
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. Senate President, Mr. Chairperson, and Honorable Members of the Senate,

3667
03:08:11,800 --> 03:08:13,320
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the National Expenditure Program,

3668
03:08:13,340 --> 03:08:17,360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: before you represents the Executive's best judgment

3669
03:08:17,360 --> 03:08:22,720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of how limited public resources can respond to the country's immediate needs

3670
03:08:22,720 --> 03:08:26,840
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: while protecting our long-term fiscal and development goals.

3671
03:08:27,240 --> 03:08:32,320
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But we also recognize that budget-making process does not end with the submission of the NEP.

3672
03:08:32,660 --> 03:08:36,380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The scrutiny of Congress is an essential part of that process.

3673
03:08:36,900 --> 03:08:40,000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The questions you will raise, the programs you examine,

3674
03:08:40,000 --> 03:08:43,140
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and the choices we make together will ultimately,

3675
03:08:43,340 --> 03:09:01,960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We will determine whether the national budget is able to deliver what our people expect from government. On the part of the DBM and the Development Budget Coordination Committee, we come before the Senate prepared to explain our assumptions, account for our recommendations, and engage constructively throughout the deliberations.

3676
03:09:01,960 --> 03:09:24,880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Because behind every number we discuss in this hearing is a consequence beyond these halls, a classroom that may be built, a hospital patient who may receive care, a farmer who may gain better access to markets, a community protected from disaster, or a Filipino family given a better opportunity to move forward.

3677
03:09:24,880 --> 03:09:31,720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: That is the standard by which this budget should ultimately be judged, not simply by how much government spends.

3678
03:09:31,960 --> 03:09:35,580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But by how much better government is able to serve.

3679
03:09:36,020 --> 03:09:50,980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We therefore look forward to working with the Senate toward a fiscal year 2027 national budget that is disciplined in its choices, credible in its commitments, transparent in its use, and meaningful in the lives of our people.

3680
03:09:51,400 --> 03:09:52,340
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Maraming salamat po.

3681
03:09:53,120 --> 03:09:56,700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Okay, thank you, Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon.

3682
