5450
05:24:56,210 --> 05:24:58,110
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: is something acceptable to everyone.

5451
05:24:58,110 --> 05:25:00,610
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So we can have a valid push

5452
05:25:00,610 --> 05:25:02,490
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: to have even more funding for next year

5453
05:25:02,490 --> 05:25:04,550
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: or at least funding that approximates

5454
05:25:04,550 --> 05:25:06,190
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: the funding that we have for this year.

5455
05:25:06,390 --> 05:25:07,470
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Certainly, Your Honor.

5456
05:25:07,570 --> 05:25:09,250
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But we would just like to add as well

5457
05:25:09,250 --> 05:25:10,450
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: that one of the considerations

5458
05:25:10,450 --> 05:25:13,070
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for classroom budget for 2027

5459
05:25:13,070 --> 05:25:15,690
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: is not only because of the current year's budget

5460
05:25:15,690 --> 05:25:17,090
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: but we're also mindful

5461
05:25:17,090 --> 05:25:19,450
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: that there is a slated PPP project

5462
05:25:19,450 --> 05:25:21,370
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for classroom building

5463
05:25:21,370 --> 05:25:23,290
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: which we target to award

5464
05:25:23,290 --> 05:25:26,030
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and to start by 2027 as well.

5465
05:25:26,030 --> 05:25:27,990
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But we commit to work with,

5466
05:25:28,110 --> 05:25:29,890
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: with Your Honor's office

5467
05:25:29,890 --> 05:25:33,050
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to ensure that we have some sufficient funding

5468
05:25:33,050 --> 05:25:34,030
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for more classrooms

5469
05:25:34,030 --> 05:25:35,430
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: because we acknowledge

5470
05:25:35,430 --> 05:25:36,650
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: that the gap is still big

5471
05:25:36,650 --> 05:25:38,830
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and the first PPP project

5472
05:25:38,830 --> 05:25:41,930
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: may not be able to cover everything.

5473
05:25:41,930 --> 05:25:43,150
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: 160,000.

5474
05:25:44,850 --> 05:25:47,250
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, see, Senator Ping was asking

5475
05:25:47,250 --> 05:25:48,890
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: what the shortage is, no?

5476
05:25:48,890 --> 05:25:51,490
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: When I entered the Senate, it was 160,000.

5477
05:25:53,130 --> 05:25:57,050
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: The national government only built 99 classrooms in 2025.

5478
05:25:57,050 --> 05:25:58,030
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: That was in our hearing.

5479
05:25:58,030 --> 05:25:58,090
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: That was in our hearing. That was in our hearing.

5480
05:25:58,090 --> 05:26:01,530
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Secretary Dizon was, I think, two weeks old.

5481
05:26:02,530 --> 05:26:04,110
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And he was also shocked by that number.

5482
05:26:05,250 --> 05:26:07,590
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: There's a commitment for almost 30,000 classrooms

5483
05:26:07,590 --> 05:26:09,590
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: by the President in the 2025 SONA,

5484
05:26:09,750 --> 05:26:10,470
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: if I'm not mistaken.

5485
05:26:11,270 --> 05:26:13,450
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: There's a huge budget for the first time

5486
05:26:13,450 --> 05:26:15,450
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: for classrooms in the 2026 budget

5487
05:26:15,450 --> 05:26:17,190
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: at 67 billion pesos.

5488
05:26:17,710 --> 05:26:19,110
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Iba pa yan sa ibang BEFF

5489
05:26:19,110 --> 05:26:20,650
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: or Basic Education Facilities.

5490
05:26:21,130 --> 05:26:23,030
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But we just haven't gotten it done.

5491
05:26:25,590 --> 05:26:27,790
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Again, Yusek Merian was at our hearing.

5492
05:26:27,790 --> 05:26:30,430
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Maraming reasons kung bakit sinabing delayed tayo.

5493
05:26:30,590 --> 05:26:32,690
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But I'm hoping, Mr. Secretary,

5494
05:26:33,070 --> 05:26:34,010
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: we can do a push.

5495
05:26:34,130 --> 05:26:36,970
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And again, binabanggit ko ulit yung 10-year education plan.

5496
05:26:37,690 --> 05:26:39,790
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kasi dyan natin makikita na kung hindi tayo pupondo

5497
05:26:39,790 --> 05:26:41,550
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: ng ganito kalaki for 10 years,

5498
05:26:42,090 --> 05:26:43,830
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: hindi natin mapupunuan yung kakulangan.

5499
05:26:44,450 --> 05:26:44,510
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: No?

5500
05:26:44,870 --> 05:26:46,710
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: The funding can't be 1 year or 2 years.

5501
05:26:46,770 --> 05:26:47,850
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: It has to be 10 years.

5502
05:26:48,470 --> 05:26:50,630
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We're scratching the surface with 67 billion.

5503
05:26:50,770 --> 05:26:52,450
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: That's only about 20,000 classrooms.

5504
05:26:52,990 --> 05:26:54,690
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: The gap is 160,000 classrooms.

5505
05:26:55,450 --> 05:26:57,330
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: By the way, this gap was almost zero

5506
05:26:57,330 --> 05:27:00,950
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: in 2018, if I'm not mistaken.

5507
05:27:01,750 --> 05:27:03,510
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So for the last 6 or 7 years,

5508
05:27:03,610 --> 05:27:04,650
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: this gap has ballooned.

5509
05:27:04,990 --> 05:27:06,250
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And every time na umuulan,

5510
05:27:06,510 --> 05:27:07,730
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: every time nagkakalindol,

5511
05:27:07,830 --> 05:27:09,010
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: every time nagkakabaha,

5512
05:27:09,830 --> 05:27:11,650
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: 1,000 classrooms at a time nasisira.

5513
05:27:12,290 --> 05:27:14,270
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So we really need to fund this, Mr. Secretary.

5514
05:27:14,530 --> 05:27:15,830
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay, let me move to something else.

5515
05:27:16,750 --> 05:27:18,490
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yung isa pong highlight in the SONA

5516
05:27:18,490 --> 05:27:22,830
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: was yung pagbanggit na gagawing tax exempt

5517
05:27:22,830 --> 05:27:25,830
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: ang 350,000 annual,

5518
05:27:26,370 --> 05:27:27,310
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: ang annual,

5519
05:27:27,330 --> 05:27:31,330
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: annual gross revenue of 350,000 and below

5520
05:27:31,330 --> 05:27:32,790
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: gagawing ng tax exempt.

5521
05:27:33,450 --> 05:27:34,790
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Secretary Goh, may I know

5522
05:27:34,790 --> 05:27:36,910
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: what is the fiscal hit

5523
05:27:36,910 --> 05:27:38,790
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: through this measure?

5524
05:27:42,560 --> 05:27:43,700
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Mr. Chair, Your Honor,

5525
05:27:43,900 --> 05:27:45,360
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: about 60 billion pesos.

5526
05:27:45,520 --> 05:27:46,020
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: 60 billion.

5527
05:27:46,620 --> 05:27:47,940
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Now, here in the Senate,

5528
05:27:48,160 --> 05:27:50,540
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I think it's Senator Gatchalian's bill,

5529
05:27:50,760 --> 05:27:52,380
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: brings it up to 400,000.

5530
05:27:53,060 --> 05:27:54,800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: My bill is actually at 480.

5531
05:27:55,740 --> 05:27:57,440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Would you have the differences?

5532
05:27:57,440 --> 05:27:59,280
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kunyari po, we did 400,

5533
05:27:59,480 --> 05:28:00,500
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: instead of 350,

5534
05:28:00,820 --> 05:28:03,140
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: or we did 480 instead of 350.

5535
05:28:04,020 --> 05:28:05,380
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: What would be the fiscal hit?

5536
05:28:05,640 --> 05:28:08,240
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Para lang we have a better understanding, no?

5537
05:28:08,820 --> 05:28:09,880
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Why do I say this?

5538
05:28:11,040 --> 05:28:11,820
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: When you look at,

5539
05:28:11,920 --> 05:28:13,860
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: and I will sound like a broken record here,

5540
05:28:14,200 --> 05:28:16,720
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: last year, pinag-usapan namin ni SecRC yung living wage.

5541
05:28:17,460 --> 05:28:18,420
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I think if I'm not mistaken,

5542
05:28:18,560 --> 05:28:20,900
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: living wage in 2026 is about,

5543
05:28:21,040 --> 05:28:23,520
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: it's close to 40,000 for a family of five.

5544
05:28:23,980 --> 05:28:25,460
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Tama po ba, Secretary Arsi?

5545
05:28:30,830 --> 05:28:31,370
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Let... let...

5546
05:28:31,710 --> 05:28:32,630
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: You'll check, you'll check.

5547
05:28:32,630 --> 05:28:33,950
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: My understanding is,

5548
05:28:33,990 --> 05:28:36,770
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: that it's anywhere from 36,000 to 40,000 pesos

5549
05:28:36,770 --> 05:28:39,730
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: ang living wage for a family of four,

5550
05:28:40,330 --> 05:28:41,510
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: or family of five, no?

5551
05:28:42,130 --> 05:28:45,330
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, tinapat ko po yung 40,000 dun sa 480,

5552
05:28:45,510 --> 05:28:47,570
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: kasi 40,000 times 12 is 480.

5553
05:28:48,470 --> 05:28:52,070
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, I know that government is supporting 350.

5554
05:28:52,870 --> 05:28:55,490
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We have other measures at 400 and 480.

5555
05:28:56,070 --> 05:28:58,410
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Could you tell us what the fiscal hit would be

5556
05:28:58,410 --> 05:28:59,510
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: kung tinaas po natin yan?

5557
05:29:00,010 --> 05:29:01,470
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yes, Mr. Chair, Your Honor.

5558
05:29:01,470 --> 05:29:03,750
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The fiscal hit at 400,000,

5559
05:29:03,990 --> 05:29:07,610
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: on the first year would be about 133 billion.

5560
05:29:08,290 --> 05:29:08,730
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So, double?

5561
05:29:08,990 --> 05:29:09,850
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Double the 350?

5562
05:29:10,630 --> 05:29:12,070
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yeah, more than double.

5563
05:29:12,310 --> 05:29:12,570
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Okay.

5564
05:29:12,830 --> 05:29:13,410
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: More than double.

5565
05:29:13,550 --> 05:29:15,550
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And at 480,000,

5566
05:29:15,970 --> 05:29:19,790
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the fiscal hit would be 143 billion pesos.

5567
05:29:19,890 --> 05:29:21,730
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, from 400 to 480, maliit lang,

5568
05:29:21,830 --> 05:29:22,730
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: mas maliit yung gap,

5569
05:29:22,830 --> 05:29:26,330
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: but the 350 to 400 is actually a huge gap.

5570
05:29:26,590 --> 05:29:27,270
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Is that correct?

5571
05:29:27,270 --> 05:29:31,230
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Ah, but, sorry, in the one,

5572
05:29:31,850 --> 05:29:33,850
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: because what we did is we copied off your,

5573
05:29:33,990 --> 05:29:35,170
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: your proposed bill.

5574
05:29:35,670 --> 05:29:36,890
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So, the one for SP,

5575
05:29:37,290 --> 05:29:38,190
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Wayne Gatchal yan,

5576
05:29:38,290 --> 05:29:40,770
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: it has a 150k bonus exemption pa.

5577
05:29:40,990 --> 05:29:41,470
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Ah, okay.

5578
05:29:41,470 --> 05:29:41,970
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: With the others.

5579
05:29:42,450 --> 05:29:42,650
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yeah.

5580
05:29:43,690 --> 05:29:43,950
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay.

5581
05:29:44,090 --> 05:29:44,790
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But, roughly,

5582
05:29:45,210 --> 05:29:46,250
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: it's double.

5583
05:29:46,430 --> 05:29:47,770
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: From 350 to 400,

5584
05:29:47,970 --> 05:29:48,430
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: it's double.

5585
05:29:48,550 --> 05:29:49,590
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: The fiscal hit will be double.

5586
05:29:49,650 --> 05:29:50,190
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: More than double.

5587
05:29:50,410 --> 05:29:50,650
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay.

5588
05:29:50,750 --> 05:29:51,110
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Thank you.

5589
05:29:51,870 --> 05:29:52,930
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And for the record,

5590
05:29:53,630 --> 05:29:55,190
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: DOF is supporting 350.

5591
05:29:55,410 --> 05:29:57,910
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Are you amenable to the 400 and the 480?

5592
05:29:59,250 --> 05:30:00,010
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Or you're confused?

5593
05:30:00,000 --> 05:30:05,000
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: My position has always been the same, Your Honor, Mr. Chair.

5594
05:30:05,580 --> 05:30:16,740
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: I am neutral to any tax erosion measure as long as we can be presented a tax revenue-generating measure.

5595
05:30:17,240 --> 05:30:21,460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So we're neutral as long as you can point us to another source.

5596
05:30:21,460 --> 05:30:28,560
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So we're okay to remove a source of tax collection as long as you point us to another source of tax collection.

5597
05:30:29,080 --> 05:30:29,240
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay.

5598
05:30:30,000 --> 05:30:40,960
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Mr. Secretary, another highlight in the SONA was the systems loss, when the President talked about systems loss.

5599
05:30:41,700 --> 05:30:46,800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I know the goal there, the most we're looking for there, is to lower the price of electricity.

5600
05:30:47,800 --> 05:30:55,600
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: At the proper time, not here, but during the hearing, during the EPIRA amendment, which is also in the LEDAC,

5601
05:30:55,600 --> 05:30:59,080
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: some of us here want to propose

5602
05:30:59,080 --> 05:31:06,780
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: instead of the systems loss, or aside from the systems loss, VAT on electricity for residential.

5603
05:31:07,600 --> 05:31:14,240
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: My understanding is that the fiscal hit for this is less than 1%, just for residential.

5604
05:31:14,800 --> 05:31:18,420
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So for, maybe this is something you can look at.

5605
05:31:18,420 --> 05:31:26,540
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: If we remove the VAT on electricity for residential, meaning not for businesses or factories, but just residential,

5606
05:31:27,060 --> 05:31:29,060
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: this could mean a bigger drop.

5607
05:31:29,840 --> 05:31:35,080
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: in the electricity bill of our citizens, and as a whole, it might be less.

5608
05:31:35,760 --> 05:31:40,240
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: because we're looking only at residential and not all consumers of electricity.

5609
05:31:40,240 --> 05:31:45,660
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Is that something you can also take a look at or help us compute, Secretary?

5610
05:31:45,660 --> 05:31:47,460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Oh, it would be our pleasure, Your Honor, to compute that for you.

5611
05:31:47,540 --> 05:31:48,040
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Uh-oh.

5612
05:31:48,040 --> 05:31:49,760
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So we're limiting the coverage.

5613
05:31:49,880 --> 05:31:58,100
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: It's not all the systems loss, just residential and then VAT, which is 12% because the systems loss is only about 5% to 6%.

5614
05:31:58,100 --> 05:31:58,900
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: With the VAT, it's a two-year period.

5615
05:31:58,900 --> 05:32:02,380
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: It's another, maybe goes up to 6, 6.5%.

5616
05:32:02,380 --> 05:32:07,920
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Pero yung VAT on electricity is 12% right away from the electricity bill.

5617
05:32:08,320 --> 05:32:09,960
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Baka this is something we can also look at.

5618
05:32:10,840 --> 05:32:15,360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay, I'm out of time, but just as a last question, yung Paxilica.

5619
05:32:17,380 --> 05:32:19,240
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Paxilica was also mentioned in the SONA.

5620
05:32:20,160 --> 05:32:26,480
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I know that in previous press releases and meetings, government has talked about this

5621
05:32:26,480 --> 05:32:28,620
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: as a major push for advanced manufacturing.

5622
05:32:29,280 --> 05:32:32,000
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Many of us want to see this manufacturing site up.

5623
05:32:32,960 --> 05:32:36,980
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Alam nyo po, ang Paxilica area is 1,600 hectares.

5624
05:32:37,780 --> 05:32:40,060
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: BGC is only 240 hectares.

5625
05:32:40,820 --> 05:32:43,060
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Anim na BGC po, ang laki nito.

5626
05:32:43,700 --> 05:32:44,940
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ang potential na laki nito.

5627
05:32:45,600 --> 05:32:49,180
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And many of us just want to be sure na kung gagawin nga natin ito,

5628
05:32:50,000 --> 05:32:52,980
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: na yung gains ng Pilipinas, ramdam na ramdam.

5629
05:32:53,300 --> 05:32:55,400
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Sa trabaho, sa teknolohiya, at iba pa.

5630
05:32:55,660 --> 05:32:56,460
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Now, in a previous press release,

5631
05:32:56,480 --> 05:32:59,480
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: in a previous hearing, headed by Senator Tulfo,

5632
05:33:00,020 --> 05:33:05,740
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: nalaman ho natin, there are about 70 to 200 families that will be affected.

5633
05:33:07,420 --> 05:33:10,360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: In the exact area where Paxilica is.

5634
05:33:10,920 --> 05:33:11,940
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I'm handling lang.

5635
05:33:12,600 --> 05:33:13,440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, lang.

5636
05:33:13,840 --> 05:33:16,560
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I'm handling the budget of BCDA.

5637
05:33:17,460 --> 05:33:23,060
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: In the budget of BCDA, nandun na po ba yung tulong para sa mga pamilyang to

5638
05:33:23,060 --> 05:33:26,280
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: para mabigyan ho natin sila ng sapat na tulong

5639
05:33:26,480 --> 05:33:34,560
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: para pwede na pong makita talaga yung pagsimula ng advanced manufacturing natin.

5640
05:33:34,920 --> 05:33:36,960
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Is that already there, Secretary Kim?

5641
05:33:37,860 --> 05:33:44,140
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, the 2027 budget across agencies does not have anything

5642
05:33:44,140 --> 05:33:47,980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: or provision for the implementation of Pax Silica.

5643
05:33:48,080 --> 05:33:53,960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But if you're looking at possibly compensation, maybe not within the subsidy of the BCDA,

5644
05:33:54,800 --> 05:33:56,460
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: but probably within their corporate funds.

5645
05:33:56,480 --> 05:33:57,220
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: If ever.

5646
05:33:57,480 --> 05:33:59,660
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But I cannot answer for certain, Your Honor.

5647
05:33:59,660 --> 05:34:03,660
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So it wouldn't be a budget item, but they could be spending for it separately.

5648
05:34:03,840 --> 05:34:03,940
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes.

5649
05:34:04,300 --> 05:34:09,920
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Because yung posisyon po ng marami ko sa amin, gusto ho namin makita yung facility na ito nakatayo.

5650
05:34:10,400 --> 05:34:13,840
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: After all, there was a commitment already that this would be advanced manufacturing

5651
05:34:13,840 --> 05:34:16,680
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: and not hyperscaler data centers.

5652
05:34:17,420 --> 05:34:18,940
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So we want to see the advanced manufacturing.

5653
05:34:19,080 --> 05:34:20,500
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We want to see the industrialization.

5654
05:34:20,500 --> 05:34:24,440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Pero ayaw ho natin na yung pinakamayihirap, yung magsasaka,

5655
05:34:25,020 --> 05:34:26,460
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: yung mga IP na nandun.

5656
05:34:26,480 --> 05:34:27,840
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ay masagasaan.

5657
05:34:28,660 --> 05:34:31,600
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Again, we're talking about 1,600 hectares.

5658
05:34:31,720 --> 05:34:35,300
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Siguro naman po we can look for space and look for support for them

5659
05:34:35,300 --> 05:34:40,420
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: to make sure that these families, hindi ho sila mapeperwisyo.

5660
05:34:40,840 --> 05:34:45,360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So we can look for that budget in the BCDA funds, not necessarily in the GAA.

5661
05:34:45,640 --> 05:34:46,440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Yes, Your Honor.

5662
05:34:46,540 --> 05:34:48,860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Not in their subsidy from the NEP, Your Honor.

5663
05:34:48,880 --> 05:34:49,060
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay.

5664
05:34:49,200 --> 05:34:55,440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: As a final point, yung isa rin pong highlight in the SONA was about restoring trust.

5665
05:34:55,480 --> 05:34:56,040
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes.

5666
05:34:56,040 --> 05:35:00,860
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And trying to put an end to corruption in our country.

5667
05:35:01,420 --> 05:35:04,040
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So as a final measure, I just want to go back and say,

5668
05:35:04,440 --> 05:35:06,900
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: sana po we pass the Kadena Law.

5669
05:35:07,180 --> 05:35:11,020
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: This is something I think that at some point, all of us were supportive of it.

5670
05:35:11,560 --> 05:35:14,840
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I'm wondering why the support has suddenly left the building.

5671
05:35:15,640 --> 05:35:16,880
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: There's an urgency to this.

5672
05:35:16,880 --> 05:35:20,980
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ayaw na po natin makita na uulan ulit, babagyo ulit, babaha ulit,

5673
05:35:21,420 --> 05:35:24,440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: na wala pang resolusyon sa mga problema natin.

5674
05:35:24,940 --> 05:35:25,660
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Just for the record,

5675
05:35:26,040 --> 05:35:28,520
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: yung pinagkaiba ng FOI tsaka nito.

5676
05:35:29,100 --> 05:35:31,120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Maganda po yung FOI, we're supporting this as well.

5677
05:35:31,600 --> 05:35:35,820
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But sa FOI, kailangan magtanong yung citizen para makuha po yung data.

5678
05:35:36,460 --> 05:35:40,800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Sa Kadena Law, lahat ng data nakalabas na ahead of time.

5679
05:35:40,900 --> 05:35:45,860
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: At nakamandato ang mga ahensya na ilabas ito as part of their work.

5680
05:35:45,860 --> 05:35:48,980
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: At kung hindi nila ilalabas ito, pwede silang makasuhan.

5681
05:35:49,980 --> 05:35:51,040
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ano po yung data?

5682
05:35:51,140 --> 05:35:55,360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Hindi lang po yung budget na nagsisimula of course with DBM hanggang sa kontrata,

5683
05:35:55,360 --> 05:35:58,100
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: sa kontraktor, sa dupa ba yun?

5684
05:35:58,240 --> 05:36:00,220
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Dupa o anong tawag doon?

5685
05:36:00,460 --> 05:36:09,920
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yung magkano yung mga simesimento, unit prices, lahat po yan, may lalabas po yan.

5686
05:36:10,000 --> 05:36:14,420
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And again, Secretary Kim, before he was a secretary, he was in NCPAG,

5687
05:36:14,520 --> 05:36:15,960
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: humihi po kami ng advice sa kanya.

5688
05:36:16,600 --> 05:36:21,120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yung isang pahina po sa batas na yun, kung ano yung mga dokumentong kailangang ilabas,

5689
05:36:21,240 --> 05:36:25,100
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: nanggaling rin po yan kay Secretary Kim de Leon, kaya we're thankful for that.

5690
05:36:25,360 --> 05:36:30,740
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So I'm hoping that if we pass this law, Secretary Kim and many of the members here,

5691
05:36:30,820 --> 05:36:34,440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: all were supportive, whether they were in or out of government,

5692
05:36:34,940 --> 05:36:37,580
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: sana po may tulak natin itong pagbabago ng sistema.

5693
05:36:38,100 --> 05:36:40,180
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And we can really make a dent against corruption.

5694
05:36:40,380 --> 05:36:47,420
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So I hope we can reconsider that and make it again a priority with regard to legislation.

5695
05:36:48,920 --> 05:36:52,080
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So ano po, SECRC, I hope we can reconsider that also.

5696
05:36:52,440 --> 05:36:54,460
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Thank you very much, Mr. Chairman. Maraming salamat.

5697
05:36:55,360 --> 05:36:56,980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Senator Aquino.

5698
05:36:58,220 --> 05:37:05,640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Actually, next is supposedly Senator Marcos, but the Senator Joel was requesting to go ahead

5699
05:37:05,640 --> 05:37:07,740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: because he has to go.

5700
05:37:09,000 --> 05:37:12,540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Actually, dapat si SP or me, pero but we have, we chose to give away.

5701
05:37:12,660 --> 05:37:18,650
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Okay, please, Senator Joel.

5702
05:37:18,690 --> 05:37:19,690
Senator Joel Villanueva: I'll be very quick.

5703
05:37:21,370 --> 05:37:25,370
Senator Joel Villanueva: I don't know how to define quick.

5704
05:37:26,650 --> 05:37:27,330
Senator Joel Villanueva: Anyway.

5705
05:37:28,530 --> 05:37:32,690
Senator Joel Villanueva: So, Mr. Chairman, kanina, when I asked that question regarding the,

5706
05:37:32,690 --> 05:37:38,970
Senator Joel Villanueva: yung primary balance na hinahanap natin for DBCC to estimate the necessary,

5707
05:37:39,230 --> 05:37:42,770
Senator Joel Villanueva: to put yung debt to GDP ratio,

5708
05:37:43,250 --> 05:37:44,850
Senator Joel Villanueva: nagtanong po sa akin, may mga nag-text,

5709
05:37:44,970 --> 05:37:46,750
Senator Joel Villanueva: hindi nasagot yata yung tanong mo,

5710
05:37:46,930 --> 05:37:50,170
Senator Joel Villanueva: pero sabi ko naman, nasagot hindi lang kompleto,

5711
05:37:50,170 --> 05:37:56,310
Senator Joel Villanueva: but just to put on record because a lot of people are also monitoring what we're doing here,

5712
05:37:56,870 --> 05:37:58,170
Senator Joel Villanueva: yung sagot po is 0.9%

5713
05:37:58,530 --> 05:38:22,690
Senator Joel Villanueva: ng deficit to GDP ratio. Right now, ang 2026 deficit is 5.45%. The target for 2028 is 3%. But the primary balance at makita natin na tumaas na papunta to that direction should be 0.9%.

5714
05:38:22,690 --> 05:38:26,330
Senator Joel Villanueva: So, yung part of my other question kanina is,

5715
05:38:26,750 --> 05:38:27,650
Senator Joel Villanueva: ano yung timeline?

5716
05:38:28,010 --> 05:38:28,510
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kailan natin?

5717
05:38:28,530 --> 05:38:35,730
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kailan natin makikita at ma-accomplish yung declining path na ito?

5718
05:38:36,130 --> 05:38:45,610
Senator Joel Villanueva: Parang hindi natin malaman at sana meron tayong vision and projection para makita natin,

5719
05:38:45,670 --> 05:38:48,210
Senator Joel Villanueva: that indeed hope springs eternal.

5720
05:38:49,150 --> 05:38:54,010
Senator Joel Villanueva: Let me go straight to the point, Mr. President, Mr. Chairman.

5721
05:38:54,490 --> 05:38:57,810
Senator Joel Villanueva: Puntahan ko unang-una yung binabanggit na,

5722
05:38:58,530 --> 05:38:59,110
Senator Joel Villanueva: living wage.

5723
05:39:00,590 --> 05:39:09,730
Senator Joel Villanueva: Article 13, Section 3 of the Constitution guarantees that all workers shall be entitled to a living wage.

5724
05:39:09,730 --> 05:39:12,230
Senator Joel Villanueva: Pero unahin ko po yung nangyayari ngayon.

5725
05:39:12,350 --> 05:39:14,850
Senator Joel Villanueva: Dito sa NCR, naki-alamang korte,

5726
05:39:15,630 --> 05:39:19,930
Senator Joel Villanueva: ang Senado nagpasa ng sense of the Senate na resolution,

5727
05:39:20,870 --> 05:39:22,390
Senator Joel Villanueva: questioning, because alam niyo ho,

5728
05:39:22,430 --> 05:39:26,190
Senator Joel Villanueva: antagal ko nang naging chair ng Senate Committee on Labor,

5729
05:39:26,410 --> 05:39:27,630
Senator Joel Villanueva: pero ngayon ko lang nakita,

5730
05:39:28,530 --> 05:39:39,810
Senator Joel Villanueva: verbatim na vinayulate ng korte yung eksaktong nakalagay sa Article 126 ng ating Labor Code.

5731
05:39:40,290 --> 05:39:41,870
Senator Joel Villanueva: Verbatim nakalagay ho doon,

5732
05:39:41,990 --> 05:39:44,730
Senator Joel Villanueva: wag makielam, wag mag-issue ng injunction,

5733
05:39:44,950 --> 05:39:48,550
Senator Joel Villanueva: wag mag-issue ng temporary restraining order.

5734
05:39:49,290 --> 05:39:51,590
Senator Joel Villanueva: Pero hanggang ngayon po, nakabimbin po ito.

5735
05:39:51,590 --> 05:39:53,390
Senator Joel Villanueva: So ang question ko una,

5736
05:39:54,050 --> 05:39:58,030
Senator Joel Villanueva: perhaps the Dept. Department can help us with this.

5737
05:39:58,030 --> 05:39:59,530
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ano ba yung position nyo dito?

5738
05:39:59,630 --> 05:40:05,490
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kasi until now, kawawan naman yung ating minimum wage earners naman po ito.

5739
05:40:05,730 --> 05:40:13,010
Senator Joel Villanueva: In fact, ano ba yung projected real purchasing power gain

5740
05:40:13,010 --> 05:40:20,510
Senator Joel Villanueva: after itong electricity, transport, rent, and food inflation through 2027?

5741
05:40:21,150 --> 05:40:22,970
Senator Joel Villanueva: Tumataas nga po yung inflation.

5742
05:40:23,710 --> 05:40:26,370
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ito nga, tinaas yung ng wage board,

5743
05:40:26,370 --> 05:40:27,370
Senator Joel Villanueva: pero may...

5744
05:40:28,030 --> 05:40:29,970
Senator Joel Villanueva: May injunction, mayroong TRO.

5745
05:40:30,690 --> 05:40:33,270
Senator Joel Villanueva: Pero kung titignan nyo naman po, kulang pa rin po eh.

5746
05:40:33,430 --> 05:40:34,410
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kulang pa rin po eh.

5747
05:40:36,390 --> 05:40:37,530
Senator Joel Villanueva: What can you say?

5748
05:40:37,710 --> 05:40:40,470
Senator Joel Villanueva: Can we get a reaction from the Department,

5749
05:40:41,310 --> 05:40:43,650
Senator Joel Villanueva: from Dept. on this particular matter?

5750
05:40:45,250 --> 05:40:48,750
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Our position, Mr. Chair, Your Honor,

5751
05:40:48,750 --> 05:40:56,890
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: is that wages, minimum wages have to be decided

5752
05:40:56,890 --> 05:40:57,750
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: at the level of the...

5753
05:40:58,030 --> 05:40:59,430
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: at the level of the...

5754
05:40:59,430 --> 05:41:01,430
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: regional tripartite bodies.

5755
05:41:02,590 --> 05:41:03,350
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So...

5756
05:41:03,350 --> 05:41:06,590
Senator Joel Villanueva: So you support the regional tripartite bodies decision?

5757
05:41:06,850 --> 05:41:09,250
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: That's our position,

5758
05:41:09,650 --> 05:41:12,750
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: that this regional tripartite bodies,

5759
05:41:13,850 --> 05:41:16,810
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: which are represented by various stakeholders,

5760
05:41:17,110 --> 05:41:18,290
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: including government.

5761
05:41:18,550 --> 05:41:19,950
Senator Joel Villanueva: Sir, I don't have much time,

5762
05:41:20,270 --> 05:41:22,390
Senator Joel Villanueva: I'll go straight to the point.

5763
05:41:22,390 --> 05:41:26,470
Senator Joel Villanueva: The minimum wage for NCR is 755.

5764
05:41:27,590 --> 05:41:27,870
Senator Joel Villanueva: And

5765
05:41:28,030 --> 05:41:34,190
Senator Joel Villanueva: In fact, dun sa bagong nilabas ng board, P840.

5766
05:41:35,610 --> 05:41:37,990
Senator Joel Villanueva: Let's look at this, NCR.

5767
05:41:38,270 --> 05:41:41,950
Senator Joel Villanueva: Will inflation erode the value of the wage increase?

5768
05:41:43,910 --> 05:41:48,730
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Well, the fact of the matter is, in the last two or three years,

5769
05:41:49,030 --> 05:41:56,530
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the increases in the minimum wages for NCR have outpaced inflation.

5770
05:41:56,530 --> 05:41:58,370
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Substantially.

5771
05:42:26,530 --> 05:42:33,170
Senator Joel Villanueva: We'll provide a more lasting, and perhaps we couldn't use the word rational standard,

5772
05:42:33,870 --> 05:42:39,370
Senator Joel Villanueva: for determining the right pay for Filipinos to afford a decent life.

5773
05:42:39,870 --> 05:42:45,470
Senator Joel Villanueva: What is the position of our economic managers on legislating a living wage?

5774
05:42:45,470 --> 05:42:51,770
Senator Joel Villanueva: Because, okay, there's a tripartite, there's a wage board,

5775
05:42:52,630 --> 05:42:54,470
Senator Joel Villanueva: but they are not all...

5776
05:42:56,530 --> 05:43:03,770
Senator Joel Villanueva: focused on that particular direction of being there,

5777
05:43:03,850 --> 05:43:06,730
Senator Joel Villanueva: in that position of having a living wage,

5778
05:43:06,830 --> 05:43:13,450
Senator Joel Villanueva: which would be fair, humane, and commensurate with the actual cost of living in this country.

5779
05:43:14,010 --> 05:43:17,410
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I have always taken the position, Mr. Chair, Your Honor,

5780
05:43:17,610 --> 05:43:23,990
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: that legislating a wage that applies for the entire country is not the right thing to do.

5781
05:43:23,990 --> 05:43:24,590
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I'm sorry?

5782
05:43:24,710 --> 05:43:24,950
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I'm sorry.

5783
05:43:25,370 --> 05:43:26,410
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Legislating a...

5784
05:43:26,530 --> 05:43:30,670
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: A minimum wage that applies for the entire country is not the right thing to do.

5785
05:43:30,870 --> 05:43:31,250
Senator Joel Villanueva: I agree.

5786
05:43:31,390 --> 05:43:31,490
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Okay.

5787
05:43:31,890 --> 05:43:41,370
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And I think that our focus should be in enhancing the employability of the workers,

5788
05:43:42,110 --> 05:43:43,310
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and enhancing...

5789
05:43:43,310 --> 05:43:47,070
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: There are two sides, because you know, for the earnings of workers,

5790
05:43:47,070 --> 05:43:49,030
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the employability of the workers,

5791
05:43:49,890 --> 05:43:55,610
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and the quality of jobs available in the market.

5792
05:43:56,010 --> 05:43:56,310
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And that means...

5793
05:43:56,530 --> 05:43:57,030
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And that means...

5794
05:43:57,030 --> 05:43:57,790
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Better investment.

5795
05:43:58,330 --> 05:44:00,370
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: You have to get those two things together.

5796
05:44:00,830 --> 05:44:05,010
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Otherwise, creating a minimum wage will just create havoc in the economy.

5797
05:44:05,650 --> 05:44:06,270
Senator Joel Villanueva: I agree.

