7139
06:49:18,310 --> 06:49:24,090
Senator Mark A. Villar: There is a point where we don't want to pass – where we don't want to exceed, because it might affect our investment-grade status.

7140
06:49:24,590 --> 06:49:29,870
Senator Mark A. Villar: And I just want to ask, what is that – more or less, as a general, what is that threshold that we do not want to exceed?

7141
06:49:30,210 --> 06:49:39,990
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: There is a World Bank threshold for general government debt-to-GDP that they have now put a number to, which is 70 percent general government debt-to-GDP.

7142
06:49:40,430 --> 06:49:42,850
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So our equivalent is 58.6.

7143
06:49:43,330 --> 06:49:47,130
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So we have a space of about 11-plus percent.

7144
06:49:47,130 --> 06:49:47,230
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Okay.

7145
06:49:48,310 --> 06:50:01,750
Senator Mark A. Villar: So are we looking at – are we looking at – what trajectory are we looking at heading into – based – of course, this – the budget this year was based – or for next year was based on certain projections.

7146
06:50:01,930 --> 06:50:06,930
Senator Mark A. Villar: So based on that, what are you projecting for our debt-to-GDP for the following year?

7147
06:50:07,710 --> 06:50:17,310
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We're projecting to go from 58.6 now to 58.4 to 58.3, all the way down to 56.1 by the year 2030.

7148
06:50:17,990 --> 06:50:18,270
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: All right.

7149
06:50:18,350 --> 06:50:18,570
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: I see.

7150
06:50:18,850 --> 06:50:19,250
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: I see.

7151
06:50:20,190 --> 06:50:24,130
Senator Mark A. Villar: And the reason why I'm asking also is, you know, I think the fiscal space is important.

7152
06:50:24,290 --> 06:50:29,790
Senator Mark A. Villar: But, you know, of course, aside from the debt increase, it's important that – what is our GDP target?

7153
06:50:30,090 --> 06:50:38,930
Senator Mark A. Villar: Because this is – I mean, what is our – because obviously, debt-to-GDP, we're not just talking about – I mean, the GDP increase will be very relevant to this number.

7154
06:50:38,930 --> 06:50:48,290
Senator Mark A. Villar: So obviously, if our debt is – if our GDP is far outpacing our debt, you know, we should be – there shouldn't be many issues.

7155
06:50:48,570 --> 06:50:57,870
Senator Mark A. Villar: But if we have a – if we continue on this low GDP, it might – it might bring us to a level that we would not want.

7156
06:50:57,870 --> 06:51:11,230
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: In real terms, Your Honor, the target GDP growth for 2027 and 2028 is 5.6.

7157
06:51:11,930 --> 06:51:12,870
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: In real terms, yeah.

7158
06:51:13,330 --> 06:51:14,350
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: 5 to 6.

7159
06:51:14,490 --> 06:51:16,090
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: 5 to 6 percent in real terms.

7160
06:51:16,110 --> 06:51:17,290
Senator Mark A. Villar: That's the target for this year.

7161
06:51:17,290 --> 06:51:17,430
Senator Mark A. Villar: Okay.

7162
06:51:18,310 --> 06:51:19,290
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: No, for next year.

7163
06:51:19,510 --> 06:51:20,750
Senator Mark A. Villar: Ah, that's the target for next year.

7164
06:51:20,830 --> 06:51:22,010
Senator Mark A. Villar: For this year, what is the target?

7165
06:51:22,490 --> 06:51:25,970
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Well, we are 3.5 to 4.5 percent.

7166
06:51:26,170 --> 06:51:26,890
Senator Mark A. Villar: For this year.

7167
06:51:27,030 --> 06:51:27,450
Senator Mark A. Villar: For this year.

7168
06:51:27,450 --> 06:51:28,110
Senator Mark A. Villar: For this year.

7169
06:51:28,610 --> 06:51:28,790
Senator Mark A. Villar: Okay.

7170
06:51:28,790 --> 06:51:37,990
Senator Mark A. Villar: And in terms of GDP growth, what – how is the – where did we see a drop?

7171
06:51:38,370 --> 06:51:40,450
Senator Mark A. Villar: Was it in consumption, government spending?

7172
06:51:40,730 --> 06:51:47,230
Senator Mark A. Villar: Was it in – which portion of the formula for GDP?

7173
06:51:47,590 --> 06:51:48,150
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It's everywhere.

7174
06:51:48,310 --> 06:51:49,930
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It's everywhere, except for net exports.

7175
06:51:50,170 --> 06:51:59,470
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Exports grew faster than imports, which is quite different this time compared to previous years.

7176
06:51:59,610 --> 06:52:00,970
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So personal consumption –

7177
06:52:00,970 --> 06:52:10,810
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Personal consumption dropped quite to something like 2 point – it slowed down – it slowed down to roughly just a little above 2 percent in the last quarter.

7178
06:52:11,070 --> 06:52:13,890
Senator Mark A. Villar: What do you attribute the drop in personal consumption?

7179
06:52:13,890 --> 06:52:17,890
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It – earlier I mentioned the weakening of – the weakening of GDP.

7180
06:52:18,310 --> 06:52:37,290
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The weakening of consumer sentiments arising from the acceleration of inflation in March, which continued – it diminished a bit, but it's still 6.2 percent as of last July.

7181
06:52:38,370 --> 06:52:45,670
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: That's still quite high compared to 2 to 3 percent – or 2 to 4 percent target.

7182
06:52:48,310 --> 06:53:10,170
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And so – and also the – I mentioned also about this concern about governance issues, the perception about our institutions and governance, and I think that that affected particularly the investment side of the equation.

7183
06:53:11,070 --> 06:53:17,570
Senator Mark A. Villar: Yes, and even the – I believe the government spending side is also quite sluggish.

7184
06:53:17,570 --> 06:53:18,070
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Yes, that – yeah.

7185
06:53:18,070 --> 06:53:24,790
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The public construction contracted by over 30 percent in two successive quarters.

7186
06:53:24,990 --> 06:53:25,970
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: That's quite sharp.

7187
06:53:26,250 --> 06:53:26,550
Senator Mark A. Villar: Yes.

7188
06:53:26,550 --> 06:53:30,750
Senator Mark A. Villar: The reason why I also want to segue into –

7189
06:53:30,750 --> 06:53:40,230
Senator Mark A. Villar: I have been helped by the law to raise the exemptions to the income tax ceiling, 300 to 360,000 pesos.

7190
06:53:42,530 --> 06:53:47,630
Senator Mark A. Villar: In my mind, if – if the government spending is low – government spending,

7191
06:53:48,070 --> 06:54:04,650
Senator Mark A. Villar: and the consumption is also low, I just – I thought that this – raising the income tax ceiling will give additional income to the lower – I guess the mid-to-lower earning segment.

7192
06:54:05,250 --> 06:54:11,510
Senator Mark A. Villar: So I thought that maybe this is a way – in my mind, it's also a way of prime-priming this.

7193
06:54:11,510 --> 06:54:15,350
Senator Mark A. Villar: And it's – in a way, instead of helping, it's also good to lower the income tax for those who – who are not doing well.

7194
06:54:15,350 --> 06:54:15,810
Senator Mark A. Villar: Yes.

7195
06:54:15,810 --> 06:54:16,410
Senator Mark A. Villar: So I think that if the government spends a lot of money, maybe it's also a way of prime-priming this.

7196
06:54:16,410 --> 06:54:16,910
Senator Mark A. Villar: Maybe it's also a way of prime-priming this.

7197
06:54:16,910 --> 06:54:17,490
Senator Mark A. Villar: So I think that if the government spends a lot of money, maybe it's also a way of prime-priming this.

7198
06:54:17,490 --> 06:54:22,910
Senator Mark A. Villar: for those who are earning less, for the lower, I guess, the lower-earning income segments.

7199
06:54:23,770 --> 06:54:27,370
Senator Mark A. Villar: And that will translate to a direct benefit in consumption

7200
06:54:27,370 --> 06:54:37,050
Senator Mark A. Villar: because that's obviously, instead of us giving out ayuda, an exemption on income tax,

7201
06:54:37,050 --> 06:54:42,650
Senator Mark A. Villar: while it will create a fiscal, I guess it will take a hit in terms of revenues,

7202
06:54:43,310 --> 06:54:46,370
Senator Mark A. Villar: but it will be compensated by an increase in consumption.

7203
06:54:46,370 --> 06:54:49,350
Senator Mark A. Villar: I suppose. I mean, I would surmise.

7204
06:54:49,630 --> 06:54:51,050
Senator Mark A. Villar: Can I ask your comment on this?

7205
06:54:52,770 --> 06:54:55,050
Senator Mark A. Villar: I'm curious because this is a bill that I filed,

7206
06:54:55,750 --> 06:55:00,810
Senator Mark A. Villar: and I wanted to know what the fiscal repercussions of this bill are,

7207
06:55:01,010 --> 06:55:02,870
Senator Mark A. Villar: what the fiscal repercussions are.

7208
06:55:06,000 --> 06:55:12,820
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And the consumption effects, I think that those certainly will be positive,

7209
06:55:12,820 --> 06:55:18,100
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: but I think the ayuda that we are talking about here,

7210
06:55:18,620 --> 06:55:18,680
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: or the...

7211
06:55:18,700 --> 06:55:26,260
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Or the effects of the tax exemptions would not reach many of the poor

7212
06:55:26,260 --> 06:55:33,800
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: who are in the informal sector, who are not paying income taxes to begin with.

7213
06:55:34,420 --> 06:55:37,400
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And many of them are poor in that category.

7214
06:55:39,000 --> 06:55:48,680
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So I think what we have seen in the last, particularly during the 2023 to 2025 period,

7215
06:55:48,700 --> 06:55:52,840
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: which is the period where we have data,

7216
06:55:53,420 --> 06:55:58,940
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: show that when done well, the ayuda could actually help,

7217
06:55:59,300 --> 06:56:07,440
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: especially those who are victims of circumstances like floods or typhoons.

7218
06:56:08,260 --> 06:56:10,940
Senator Mark A. Villar: Actually, I'm not saying that there should be no ayuda.

7219
06:56:11,080 --> 06:56:12,640
Senator Mark A. Villar: The ayuda is okay, I'm just saying.

7220
06:56:12,640 --> 06:56:15,640
Senator Mark A. Villar: Maybe for the lower...

7221
06:56:16,260 --> 06:56:18,040
Senator Mark A. Villar: Maybe it's also good that...

7222
06:56:18,040 --> 06:56:18,620
Senator Mark A. Villar: Maybe it's also good that...

7223
06:56:18,620 --> 06:56:20,320
Senator Mark A. Villar: Maybe it's also good that we also have the lower income segment.

7224
06:56:20,500 --> 06:56:23,280
Senator Mark A. Villar: We don't have what we call D, E.

7225
06:56:23,480 --> 06:56:25,340
Senator Mark A. Villar: We also have the lower income segment.

7226
06:56:25,940 --> 06:56:28,420
Senator Mark A. Villar: Maybe we also need to give relief.

7227
06:56:28,900 --> 06:56:37,480
Senator Mark A. Villar: And in my opinion, income tax is also a big relief for people earning less than P360,000 a year.

7228
06:56:37,600 --> 06:56:38,800
Senator Mark A. Villar: I mean, this is not...

7229
06:56:38,800 --> 06:56:41,240
Senator Mark A. Villar: Generally, these are people who do pay taxes.

7230
06:56:41,380 --> 06:56:43,800
Senator Mark A. Villar: They're minimum wage earners who pay taxes.

7231
06:56:43,800 --> 06:56:46,340
Senator Mark A. Villar: But if we can give some of them some tax relief,

7232
06:56:47,000 --> 06:56:47,800
Senator Mark A. Villar: in my opinion, it's not just...

7233
06:56:48,620 --> 06:56:52,360
Senator Mark A. Villar: I understand that there's something right in the government's revenues.

7234
06:56:53,260 --> 06:56:59,220
Senator Mark A. Villar: But at the same time, this is a way of giving instant relief to many of our taxpayers

7235
06:56:59,220 --> 06:57:03,520
Senator Mark A. Villar: who also need a lot of our low-income tax earners.

7236
06:57:03,720 --> 06:57:04,880
Senator Mark A. Villar: Low-income earners.

7237
06:57:05,680 --> 06:57:07,220
Senator Mark A. Villar: Mid to low-income earners.

7238
06:57:07,220 --> 06:57:10,220
Senator Mark A. Villar: So, I just want to...

7239
06:57:10,900 --> 06:57:17,240
Senator Mark A. Villar: I hope you can maybe compute what the net benefit is if we lose some of our revenues.

7240
06:57:17,740 --> 06:57:18,460
Senator Mark A. Villar: But at the same time...

7241
06:57:18,460 --> 06:57:20,580
Senator Mark A. Villar: At the same time, may madadagdag din sa consumption.

7242
06:57:20,840 --> 06:57:21,940
Senator Mark A. Villar: And this is a...

7243
06:57:21,940 --> 06:57:24,020
Senator Mark A. Villar: For me, it's a progressive reform.

7244
06:57:24,260 --> 06:57:25,460
Senator Mark A. Villar: Kasi lahat mabibigyan eh.

7245
06:57:26,140 --> 06:57:27,460
Senator Mark A. Villar: Wala nang inefficiency.

7246
06:57:27,840 --> 06:57:31,180
Senator Mark A. Villar: Hindi na natin pipiliin kung kanina natin ibibigay yung ayuda.

7247
06:57:31,660 --> 06:57:37,740
Senator Mark A. Villar: Ito directly to people who need immediate relief, I think.

7248
06:57:38,400 --> 06:57:39,740
Senator Mark A. Villar: That's just my theory.

7249
06:57:40,080 --> 06:57:41,220
Senator Mark A. Villar: And that's my belief.

7250
06:57:41,220 --> 06:57:46,420
Senator Mark A. Villar: So, I want to ask your comments, Mr. Chairman, on these thoughts.

7251
06:57:56,020 --> 06:57:56,900
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I would say that...

7252
06:57:57,140 --> 06:58:02,160
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The net benefits, I don't think that the first-round effects on consumption,

7253
06:58:02,840 --> 06:58:08,640
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: additional consumption and additional revenue that that consumption would generate,

7254
06:58:09,020 --> 06:58:12,740
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: would be able to offset what you give away.

7255
06:58:13,220 --> 06:58:16,260
Senator Mark A. Villar: Do we know how much more or less revenues is generated?

7256
06:58:16,260 --> 06:58:23,560
Senator Mark A. Villar: What would be the effect on our revenues of that tax like that on the lower-income segment?

7257
06:58:25,820 --> 06:58:26,620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Mr. Chair?

7258
06:58:26,920 --> 06:58:27,080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yes.

7259
06:58:27,140 --> 06:58:29,060
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Since that's directly a DOF question.

7260
06:58:29,060 --> 06:58:38,560
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: I think, for example, in our proposal to raise the personal income tax exemption to 350,000 a year,

7261
06:58:38,840 --> 06:58:42,140
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we're estimating to lose about 60 billion in taxes.

7262
06:58:42,700 --> 06:58:47,840
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And we will probably recover only somewhere around 15% of that in taxes.

7263
06:58:48,920 --> 06:58:57,100
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The reason for that is the highest level of consumption at that income bracket will be food.

7264
06:58:57,140 --> 06:59:07,760
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And a lot of the food-related are exempted, for example, from VAT, and there's a lot of exemptions at that level.

7265
06:59:10,480 --> 06:59:10,900
Senator Mark A. Villar: Yes.

7266
06:59:11,500 --> 06:59:13,980
Senator Mark A. Villar: That's why I think when it comes to...

7267
06:59:13,980 --> 06:59:19,900
Senator Mark A. Villar: Of course, obviously, in the ecosystem of government, once you collect, you will have to redisperse it somehow.

7268
06:59:19,900 --> 06:59:22,120
Senator Mark A. Villar: And there are efficiencies.

7269
06:59:22,120 --> 06:59:27,700
Senator Mark A. Villar: If the government spending is low, as it has been,

7270
06:59:28,480 --> 06:59:39,000
Senator Mark A. Villar: I was just saying, perhaps we might consider these tax exemptions as a more efficient way to give assistance to those who may need it.

7271
06:59:39,120 --> 06:59:43,840
Senator Mark A. Villar: Because it's, like, again, I said, in a way, we can see it as a little bit more progressive.

7272
06:59:44,460 --> 06:59:51,760
Senator Mark A. Villar: It's not bound by inefficiencies in distribution or bureaucratic inefficiencies.

7273
06:59:51,760 --> 06:59:57,940
Senator Mark A. Villar: It's just a clear cut that goes directly to the spending.

7274
06:59:58,480 --> 07:00:00,000
Senator Mark A. Villar: I guess it goes directly...

7275
07:00:00,000 --> 07:00:07,680
Senator Mark A. Villar: to the income of our lower earning, lower income segment.

7276
07:00:09,080 --> 07:00:13,440
Senator Mark A. Villar: So I just hope this is something that we can compute.

7277
07:00:13,580 --> 07:00:16,420
Senator Mark A. Villar: I hope I can ask, maybe the effect is 60 billion,

7278
07:00:16,600 --> 07:00:20,320
Senator Mark A. Villar: but I mean, when you talk about in a nationwide scale,

7279
07:00:21,060 --> 07:00:23,900
Senator Mark A. Villar: there are a lot of people who will benefit from this bill.

7280
07:00:24,460 --> 07:00:27,420
Senator Mark A. Villar: Of course, in terms, it is so immediately, and it's immediate.

7281
07:00:27,420 --> 07:00:31,280
Senator Mark A. Villar: You don't have to wait for it to be distributed, there's no bureaucracy.

7282
07:00:31,980 --> 07:00:36,100
Senator Mark A. Villar: The moment you pass this bill, immediately, those who are earning less than 30,000

7283
07:00:36,100 --> 07:00:39,460
Senator Mark A. Villar: will have immediate relief to many people.

7284
07:00:39,640 --> 07:00:43,100
Senator Mark A. Villar: So I hope that can be given a very strong consideration,

7285
07:00:43,360 --> 07:00:46,220
Senator Mark A. Villar: and hopefully, you can support the bill.

7286
07:00:46,660 --> 07:00:52,520
Senator Mark A. Villar: Because I think there's something right, but for me, it's also worth it.

7287
07:00:54,140 --> 07:00:57,000
Senator Mark A. Villar: We can generate additional income.

7288
07:00:57,200 --> 07:00:57,400
Senator Mark A. Villar: Maybe.

7289
07:00:57,420 --> 07:01:03,000
Senator Mark A. Villar: Maybe from our GCCs, if we can generate 60 billion from our GCCs,

7290
07:01:03,260 --> 07:01:05,960
Senator Mark A. Villar: and we can pass this bill, I think it would be great

7291
07:01:05,960 --> 07:01:10,400
Senator Mark A. Villar: if we can increase the income tax exemption ceiling.

7292
07:01:10,560 --> 07:01:17,740
Senator Mark A. Villar: So I hope that can be considered by the economic team.

7293
07:01:19,740 --> 07:01:20,940
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: If I may, yeah.

7294
07:01:21,540 --> 07:01:24,300
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I think another way of looking at it is,

7295
07:01:24,300 --> 07:01:27,400
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the last time we revised,

7296
07:01:27,420 --> 07:01:32,480
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the tax rates was 2018, was it?

7297
07:01:32,960 --> 07:01:33,700
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Yeah, 2018.

7298
07:01:34,100 --> 07:01:36,420
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And there has been so much inflation since then.

7299
07:01:37,120 --> 07:01:42,420
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: You see, so that those groups of population in that bracket

7300
07:01:42,420 --> 07:01:48,640
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: are now paying much higher, effectively, much higher taxes than in 2018.

7301
07:01:49,260 --> 07:01:52,860
Senator Mark A. Villar: So in a way, it's an inflationary adjustment.

7302
07:01:53,220 --> 07:01:55,300
Senator Mark A. Villar: That's a good way to look at it, Secretary.

7303
07:01:55,300 --> 07:01:57,060
Senator Mark A. Villar: So we're basically,

7304
07:01:57,420 --> 07:02:03,840
Senator Mark A. Villar: actually this bill is just adjusting it to the realities of the past years of inflation.

7305
07:02:04,520 --> 07:02:05,360
Senator Mark A. Villar: That's another way.

7306
07:02:05,400 --> 07:02:07,900
Senator Mark A. Villar: That's a very good way to look at it, Secretary.

7307
07:02:08,100 --> 07:02:09,940
Senator Mark A. Villar: So maybe as part of the,

7308
07:02:10,560 --> 07:02:15,120
Senator Mark A. Villar: I hope that the Department of Finance will also consider that as a,

7309
07:02:15,660 --> 07:02:18,400
Senator Mark A. Villar: it would be a big, I think it would be,

7310
07:02:18,680 --> 07:02:20,300
Senator Mark A. Villar: I think it would be,

7311
07:02:20,300 --> 07:02:23,360
Senator Mark A. Villar: a big help to our countrymen.

7312
07:02:23,600 --> 07:02:26,440
Senator Mark A. Villar: And this help will be given immediately.

7313
07:02:26,440 --> 07:02:32,060
Senator Mark A. Villar: So it's a big deal if we pass this bill.

7314
07:02:56,440 --> 07:03:00,540
Senator Mark A. Villar: Defended a few years ago is the Maharlika.

7315
07:03:01,700 --> 07:03:06,120
Senator Mark A. Villar: Gusto ko sanang humingi ng update kung ano po yung mga investments ng Maharlika

7316
07:03:06,120 --> 07:03:10,700
Senator Mark A. Villar: at kung ano ng performance ng Maharlika Investment Fund.

7317
07:03:48,810 --> 07:03:50,410
